From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-fbd: screenshots on request (fbshot)

`rpi-fbd shot <file>` (and `fbshot`) asks the running rpi-fbd for the
buffer on screen as a PPM file and prints its size, top-colour share and
number of colours, for tests without a person on boards without network
(Pi 400, QEMU raspi4b). rpi-fbd looks for the request every 500 ms; the
EDID is still read every 5 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
