 //!
 //! With two buffers it waits for the vertical blank after a flip before
 //! drawing into the buffer that was shown, unless `RPI_FB_VSYNC=off`.
+//!
+//! `rpi-fbd shot [file.ppm]` (installed as `fbshot` too) is a screenshot
+//! for tests without a person: it asks the running `rpi-fbd` for the
+//! buffer on screen as a PPM file (`shot.rs`) and prints its size, the
+//! share of the most common colour and the number of colours, since the
+//! Pi 400 and QEMU's raspi4b have no network to fetch the file over.
 
